{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdgTbnJkggk7VxAe7rsX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PNxyvQ5twTPMTYV4N1qX8t","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop; D=iter_3/candidate_5\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nsrc = open(\"models/personal_memory_capacity_blur.py\").read()\ndoc_old = src.split('\"\"\"')[1]\ndoc_new = \"\"\"Refinement of `personal_memory_capacity_blur`: personal capacity blur plus a personal antisymmetry weight.\n\nEach person still holds both sequences in working memory with their own\ncapacity, so the comparison is divided by sqrt(1 + (n / K_i)^2) and long pairs\nare judged less sharply by low-capacity people; the impression is still the\ncurrent best judgement (personal ideal switching rate and sensitivity with an\nasymmetric tolerance, personal weights on imbalance and the longest run,\nshared weights on the final run, mirror symmetry, run-length variety and the\nmost lopsided stretch, and a personal lapse rate). The one change is grafting\nin the incumbent's personal complement-symmetry aversion: noticing that a\nsequence equals its own reverse with heads and tails swapped is a personal\ntrait (a weight per person drawn from a population) rather than shared.\n\"\"\"\nsrc = src.replace(doc_old, doc_new, 1)\nold = '''    chi = pm.Normal(\"chi\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.5)\n'''\nnew = '''    mu_chi = pm.Normal(\"mu_chi\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.5)\n    sigma_chi = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_chi\", sigma=1.0)\n    z_chi = pm.Normal(\"z_chi\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=MAX_PARTICIPANTS)\n    chi = mu_chi + sigma_chi * z_chi\n'''\nassert old in src\nsrc = src.replace(old, new)\nsrc = src.replace(\"    b = beta[participant_id]\\n\", \"    b = beta[participant_id]\\n    c = chi[participant_id]\\n\")\nassert src.count(\"- chi * antisym_\") == 2\nsrc = src.replace(\"- chi * antisym_\", \"- c * antisym_\")\nopen(\"iter_3/candidate_5/candidate.py\", \"w\").write(src)\nEOF\ncat > $D/hypothesis.md <<'EOF'\nRefinement of `personal_memory_capacity_blur` (statistically tied with the best): each person still has their own working-memory capacity, so their impression of which sequence looks more random decides the choice sharply for short pairs but is blurred for pairs whose length approaches or exceeds that capacity, and the impression is still the current best judgement (personal ideal switching rate and sensitivity with lenience toward over-alternation, personal weights on imbalance and the longest streak, shared weights on the final streak, mirror symmetry, run-length variety and the most lopsided stretch, and a personal guessing rate). The one change is grafting in the incumbent's personal complement-symmetry aversion: whether a sequence that equals its own reverse with heads and tails swapped (HHTT, HTHTHTHT, HHHTHTTT) looks deliberately constructed is each person's own trait rather than shared — so the two personal sources of consistency (memory capacity, concentrated on long pairs, and noticing antisymmetry, concentrated on antisymmetric pairs) are estimated together, addressing the critique (surviving FDR) that people differ in how often they agree with the majority more than the incumbent produces.\nEOF\necho capacity_blur_personal_antisymmetry > $D/model_name.txt\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run1/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_5 --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creatio